<title>FRANCE: Elf sells Tunisian assets. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>Elf sells Tunisian assets. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Elf Aquitaine SA said on Monday it had signed a deal to sell its Tunisian unit Elf Hydrocarbures Tunisie to ARCO.</p>
<p>EHT holds interests in different fields in Tunisia with its share of production amounting to 9,200 barrels of oil equivalent per day in 1996, principally from the offshore field of Ashtart where it has a 50 percent stake with Tunisian company ETAP.</p>
<p>Tunisia represented some one percent of Elf's oil production, net of royalties, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>(Corrects to show Tunisia represents one percent of Elf's production, not reserves.)</p>
<p>Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
</text>
